# Git workflow

Full policy: [docs/development/branching-strategy.md](../../docs/development/branching-strategy.md), [docs/development/commit-guidelines.md](../../docs/development/commit-guidelines.md).

## Branches

- Branch from up-to-date `main`.
- Use short-lived branches: `feat/`, `fix/`, `docs/`, `chore/`, `test/`, `refactor/`, `ci/`, `security/`.
- Delete the branch after merge. Do not accumulate long-lived feature branches.
- Never force-push `main`. Do not skip git hooks unless the user explicitly requests it.

## Commits

- Conventional Commits: `type(scope): summary` in imperative mood.
- Types: `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `style`, `refactor`, `perf`, `test`, `build`, `ci`, `chore`, `revert`.
- Scopes when useful: `web`, `api`, `worker`, `db`, `auth`, `sbom`, `policy`, `intel`, `security`, `docs`.
- Breaking changes use `!` after the type/scope and a `BREAKING CHANGE:` footer.
- Do not commit secrets, `.env` files, or real SBOMs. Do not rewrite unrelated files.

## Pull requests

Required before merge (once CI exists; until then, run the equivalent locally and report actual results):

- Lint and TypeScript check
- Unit and integration tests for touched behavior
- Relevant Playwright coverage for user-visible web changes
- Review against [docs/development/review-checklist.md](../../docs/development/review-checklist.md)
- ADR when the change is an architecture decision

Do not merge with skipped tests unless a tracked reason is documented. Do not describe the tree as production-ready merely because checks passed.
